
# basePath Chapter4

::FirstContractOpenCh4 
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene
@once 

{@Dorian}    I've got to head out. That was fun. 
{@Player}    Thanks for visiting. We need a rematch soon!

// New optional research sample- Gold
{@Xavier}    Locke! Heard about the slowdowns at Kalvis. Copper prices are through the roof!
{@Xavier}    Terrible news for Kalvis. Golden opportunity for you.
{@Xavier}    Which is why I'm sending you a little sample, straight from the Planet of Gold and Golden Opportunities.
{@Player}    Blaze and the others are doing the best they can. It's not their fault the automation and bots keep fritzing out.
{@Xavier}    Well, here in the COMPETENTLY managed, Frontier-supported Ralston system, our bots are humming along...

//end call

{@PAL}       That call appears to have ended prematurely.




//end call

::BeforeSupplyChainCh4
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research), IsSolutionFoundFor(Design)
@cutscene 
@once 

//quinn will introduce the idea that the hauling region you need is larger. She wants you to connect to callie to make sure she's willing to deal with you since you are frontier now. 

//incoming call from quinn
//incoming call from quinn
{@Quinn}    I saw what those Frontier folks on Frosch are charging you for boron.
{@Player}   Yeah. They love those high prices.
{@Quinn}    I know someone who can beat that price. By a lot.
{@Quinn}    But working with Callie can be a little... risky.
{@Quinn}    Umm... so, when you talk to her, try not to offend her.

//end call

//call callie

{@Callie}   A'hoy! I see a Frontier call sign... how scandalous. 
{@Callie}   Be blessed in my presence mere corpo-lackey! Or as I like to call ye, Clackey!
{@Callie}  	It is I, the Boron Space Pirate Queen of Velos Station! 
{@Player}  	Nice to meet you... Callie. 
{@Callie}   Since the great revolt of the Velos Penal Station...
{@Callie}   ...all Frontier ships are marked for pillaging!
{@Callie}   If you do business with us... We may avert our attention. 
{@Callie}   Holler if you need some goods, Clackey. 
//end call

{@Player}  	Hey! I'm not a Clackey- aaaand she hung up. 

{@Pal}    	Wait. Velos? The pirate station? The prison station?
{@Player}   Yeah. Looks like they have great prices.
{@Player}   How risky could it really be?
{@Pal}      They're pirates, Locke.




